    {
      "table": "articles",
      "key": {
        "provision_id": "A1"
      },
      "field": "rule",
      "proposed": "AUTHORITY:within the governed project,the current authoritative Codex is the sole normative authority and sole source of governing principles. UNITY:general provisions,special laws and express exceptions are parts of that same Codex,not parallel authorities. DERIVATION:all governance decisions,permissions,implementation rules and business rules must derive from and remain subordinate to applicable current Codex principles;no registry,configuration,contract,manual,engine,model,mirror or evidence record can independently create,replace or override law. OWNERSHIP:an assigned owner administers or executes only powers granted by the Codex;custody,storage,decision and execution authority are bounded responsibilities,not alternative legislative authority. CHANGE:human-governor-directed amendments acquire legal effect only through the governed current successor and preserved lineage;an external instruction or operational artifact cannot silently amend the current Codex. CONFLICT:an inconsistent external rule has no authority to displace the controlling principle;affected actions fail closed pending governed resolution. CONTENT:B5 limits law to principles;implementation and business rules remain outside law without acquiring independent normative authority."
    },
    {
      "table": "articles",
      "key": {
        "provision_id": "A1"
      },
      "field": "prohibition",
      "proposed": "FORBID:parallel-normative-authority+external-rule-overriding-Codex+registry-or-engine-created-law+owner-self-legislation+mirror-as-authority+implicit-amendment+special-law-as-independent-Codex+implementation-or-business-rule-as-law"
    },
    {
      "table": "articles",
      "key": {
        "provision_id": "B5"
      },
      "field": "rule",
      "proposed": "SCOPE:the Codex records principles only,including legitimate authority,ownership boundaries,separation of duties,permission,data custody,isolation,safety,accountability,evidence,independent verification,interpretation and governed change. EXCLUSION:implementation rules and business rules do not enter the Codex;algorithms,programming languages,software stacks,files,paths,APIs,schemas,protocol layouts,technical versions,model topology,parameters,thresholds,test-suite composition,scheduling procedures and business decision procedures belong to their governed owners outside the Codex. APPLICABILITY:this boundary controls every general provision,special law,ordinance and purported normative registry payload;registration,format or writing style cannot turn an excluded detail into a legal principle. EXTERNAL-OWNERSHIP:owner-local contracts,policies,configuration and business specifications are subordinate operational artifacts,not independent normative authorities;their validity and permitted effects derive exclusively from applicable current Codex principles and granted ownership.They cannot create legal duties,enlarge permissions,override a principle or establish another law source. REFERENCES:the Codex may identify the responsible owner and controlling principle without importing the external rule payload or making an implementation choice a legal mandate. LEGACY:excluded details remaining in existing records are non-operative legacy material for lawful owner-local migration,not current Codex authority;principles contained in a mixed record remain binding. MIGRATION:migration requires attributable ownership,evidence and independent validation;unresolved custody or equivalence remains incomplete and cannot be declared complete by relabeling. SAFETY:separating principles from implementation does not waive current permissions,approved safety controls,independent verification or release gates;uncertain authority fails closed. AUTHORITY:A1 establishes the current authoritative Codex as the sole normative authority;only its governed current principles have legal effect.General law,special law and express exceptions remain within the one Codex;translations,mirrors,registries,external rules,implementation projections and audit measurements create no additional law."
    },
